<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bogotá</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Santa Fe de Bogotá</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bogotá, founded as Santa Fe de Bogotá by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gonzalo-jimenez-de-quesada">Gonzalo Jiménez de Quesada</a> in 1538 on the high plain of the Muisca, became the capital of the Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>. From the 18th century it was the seat of the Viceroyalty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-granada">New Granada</a>, and after independence it became the capital of Colombia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bogota.jpg" alt="Bogotá" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pedro Szekely from Los Angeles, USA · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bogota,_Colombia_(36668708290).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
